{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact combined IE-1 and FG-1 head e1cf5adb8b8147a35aaabd10afc7de6a6fb4c53b on builder/ie1-fg1-derive-20261113, all 11 artifacts, for review request 0088a01f under IE-1 promise 204cf1a3 (request 586475dc) and FG-1 promise 9adca452 (request 212e97dd). Both changes are small and exact, and the gate evidence holds.\n\nIE-1, `packages/derive/src/item-effects.ts`. `isItemEffect(effect: Effect | GenesisEffect): effect is ItemEffect` tests `Object.hasOwn` on `ITEM_EFFECT_KINDS`. That map is `as const satisfies Record\u003cItemEffect[\"effect\"], true\u003e`, so a kind added to `ItemEffect` and missing from the map fails to compile, and an extra key fails too. `Object.hasOwn` doesn't read inherited names such as `constructor`. `fold.ts` re-exports the guard. `applyEntry` keeps its signature, as request 586475dc requires. The test names each of the six item effects and the nine other kinds. The post-gate record shows that removing the type predicate gives the one intended TS2322 at `item-effects.test.ts(7,87)`.\n\nFG-1, `packages/derive/src/fold.ts:82-83`. A genesis whose seed names a digest other than the pinned definition's digest throws `FoldError(\"the genesis seed names another definition\")`, before `resolvedEntryEffects` and before any write. A seed that names a platform definition, such as `platform:directory@1`, isn't a digest, so it folds as before. `fold-genesis-seed.test.ts` witnesses both cases: the refusal, the matching digest, and a platform name that gives the same items as the declared definition. The post-gate control shows the refusal case failing exactly its `toThrow` assertion without the guard, and the platform case passing.\n\nThe post-gate commit, 54a1bcb5. `git diff 983deef1 e1cf5adb -- packages/derive/test/item-effects.test.ts` changes one comment line and nothing else. The old line claimed that a new kind of `Effect` fails the count until the test names it. That holds only for a new member of the witness list, not for a new member of the union. The new line says only that the inventory holds all 15 kinds. Ruling 73ac2bda permits the change. Every other path that differs from the gate checkpoint is under `notes/`.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 5b342ee9 is an ancestor of the head and of the gate checkpoint 983deef1. Against main, the head changes 8 paths, and the 11 artifacts cover every one: 8 path artifacts and the 3 FG-1 companions for `fold.ts`, `fold-genesis-seed.test.ts` and the note. The request names 64885322 as the primary and calls it the implementation note. That artifact covers `notes/implementation/evidence/2026-11-14-ie1-fg1-doc-checks.manifest.json`. The note's artifact is faa2ff75, and `gs review` binds the implementations to that report, so I file faa2ff75 first.\n- Evidence. The three manifests have the digests that the request states: 3a829d39 (gate, 44 files), 58a719ec (post-gate, 48 files) and 2a2fdc33 (document checks, 10 files). All 102 files match their SHA-256 values, and none is missing.\n  - The gate's `SHA256SUMS` verifies. `gate.exit` is 0, and `head.txt` names 983deef1 with tree fa59cbdb.\n  - `gate.stdout` ends \"gate passed\" with no timeout line.\n  - All 55 power samples, from 00:54 to 01:12 EST, read AC Power, and power mode is 0 at START and END. The host's `pmset -g log` shows no sleep or wake from 00:50 to 01:15. The gate ended before the cutover window opened at 01:17.\n- The capture-helper failure. The outer helper expected exit 2 from the compiler mutant, got 1, and so exited 1 itself. The compiler's own exit 1 and its single TS2322 diagnostic are the intended results, and the post-gate manifest seals both. I accept the record as disclosed: the helper's expectation was wrong, and the checks it ran completed.\n- Cheap checks at the head. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (7 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean. As the request asks, I ran no gate, compiler or test beside CUT-A's slot.\n\nKernel review under `docs/kernel.md` section 7: no objection. Both changes sit in `packages/derive`, which is kernel. Ruling 8f63f164 permits both changes and the wider guard signature. `isItemEffect` is a new export, a pure predicate over existing types. The fold refusal enforces the rule of section 6.1 that the genesis judge (`genesisJudged`) already applies, so the fold now refuses what the judge refuses. A journal that the judge admitted never meets it. The head adds no scope kind, platform definition, capability, `RefusalReason` member or journal form.\n\nArchitecture: sound. An adapter now asks one exported guard instead of copying the item-effect list, and the compiler keeps the guard and the type together. The fold no longer trusts its caller to pin the definition that the seed names.\n\nSecurity: no finding. Before FG-1, a caller that folded a recorded genesis under another declared definition got a state built by the wrong rules, with no error. Replay and the client replica now get a `FoldError` instead. A platform name still folds without that check. The genesis judge and the pin resolution keep that check for platform scopes, as before.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing or deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:faa2ff75343351af216fce692fe4e08b408543b0","binding":"assigned","head":"e1cf5adb8b8147a35aaabd10afc7de6a6fb4c53b","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ca074a5de594e4a16c7a04120ad13ba9a2cb6c5f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:204cf1a3587e6ddb9fe6f85a9cc1ea3ef093fb49\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9adca452c90c1e95954735ff17120271ef310fb6\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dbf4388930ab68881a2f4c08a8cbe3b41d39102c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}